# p_4a7c — Marco's Minimal Commute: Everything Stays in the House

Marco works afternoon-to-night shifts, out from roughly 1:40 PM until 11 PM on weekdays. Despite the long absence, his personal effects do not travel with him. The scarf hangs on the entry hook, the umbrella stands on the entry floor, the lunchbox sits in the kitchen cupboard, the keys rest on the entry floor, and the wallet and sunglasses stay on the entry table. The robot's repeated looks during 9–17 h confirm: these items are present at their usual spots even while Marco is at work.

Two objects do move during the day. The journal shifts from the nightstand to the bedroom desk around 1 PM (a last entry before he leaves, or Yuki relocates it) and returns to the nightstand by 7 PM. His glasses sit on the nightstand overnight, move to the bathroom shelf around 9 AM (he showers and sets them there), and stay on the shelf through the afternoon before returning to the nightstand in the evening. His vitamins sit on the kitchen counter all day, with a brief appearance at the kitchen table around 10 AM when he takes them with his morning coffee.

This hypothesis sets itself apart from p_b7c2 (which sends the lunchbox, vitamins, and journal out of the house) and from p_a1b2, p_c3d4, p_e5f6, and p_7890 (which send the scarf and umbrella out). If any of Marco's personal items are sighted OUT_OF_HOUSE during 14:00–22:00 on a weekday, this document is refuted. If the journal is found at the nightstand at 15:00 on a weekday, the desk block is wrong.

