# p_c5d9 — Thursday Evening: Friends at the Table, Kitchen in Overdrive

The residents announced on Thursday that friends are coming over this evening. This single social event reshapes the afternoon and evening: the kitchen is in overdrive from 12:00 onward, the kitchen table is set for six or more, serving dishes and extra plates and glasses come out of the cupboard, and the baking tray (already at the kitchen table by 14:00 on a normal weekday) stays out because it is being used to carry food to the table. Marco likely comes home earlier than his usual 11 PM—perhaps by 6:30 or 7:00—to help set up and greet guests. The dog bowl is moved from the kitchen floor to the living room floor so the dog is not underfoot while people gather. The board game comes off the bookshelf and onto the coffee table or kitchen table for post-dinner entertainment. The candle on the coffee table is lit for the evening.

On a normal weekday the baking tray is at the pantry shelf 00:00–10:00, briefly at the counter at 12:00, then at the kitchen table 14:00–16:00, and back at the pantry by 18:00. On Thursday it stays at the kitchen table through the evening (14:00–22:00) because it is in active use for the gathering. The serving dish, which normally stays in the cupboard all day, appears at the kitchen table from 18:00. Extra plates and glasses are out of the cupboard and on the table from 17:00.

This hypothesis is specific to Thursday (and any day with a similar social event). It is refuted if the baking tray is at the pantry shelf at 18:00 on Thursday, if the serving dish is in the cupboard at 19:00 on Thursday, or if the board game is on the bookshelf at 20:00 on Thursday. On non-Thursday days, the baking tray and serving dish return to their normal resting spots.

